                     "value": "1. Codec selection\n\nThe server selects the codec from the request Content-Type. application/grpc+erlpack selects GRPC.Codec.Erlpack when the server registers it. No authentication step comes before this.\n\n2. Size limit on compressed bytes only\n\nThe server limits the request body with max_body_size, which counts the bytes received. With the gRPC compressed flag set to 0, the transport decompression limit does not apply, and the message reaches the codec unchanged.\n\n3. Expansion inside binary_to_term/2\n\nGRPC.Codec.Erlpack.decode/2 calls :erlang.binary_to_term(binary, [:safe]). The Erlang external term format has a compressed form (version byte 131, tag 80, a 32-bit uncompressed size, then a zlib stream). binary_to_term/2 inflates it in full, and the :safe option does not limit the size. ensure_safe_term!/1 runs after the call returns and accepts a large binary.\n\n4. Result\n\nIn a test against grpc_server 1.0.6, a 260,932-byte request body decoded to a 268,435,456-byte binary, which the server passed to the application callback."
                 }
