                     "value": "1. The header selects the clause\n\nThe Cowboy handler derives the access mode from the request Content-Type. application/json selects :http_transcoding, application/grpc selects :grpc and application/grpc-web+proto selects :grpcweb. The router still matches the transcoded URL template and extracts its path bindings.\n\n2. Bindings are applied in one clause only\n\nGRPC.Server.do_handle_request/4 reads the bindings with adapter.get_bindings/1 and merges them through GRPC.Server.Transcode.map_request/5 only in the :http_transcoding clause. The unary and request-streaming clauses decode the body alone with the selected codec. GRPC.Codec.Proto is in the default codecs of every server, so application/grpc is always accepted.\n\n3. The HTTP/1.1 guard never matches\n\nresolve_access_mode/3 has a clause that forces transcoding for HTTP/1.1 requests. It matches the version as the binary \"HTTP/1.1\", while Cowboy stores the version as an atom, so the clause never applies and the request works over plain HTTP/1.1.\n\n4. Result\n\nA request to /v1/messages/alice with Content-Type: application/grpc and a message that sets name to victim reaches the handler with name set to victim. With an empty message the field is empty: the path binding is never consulted."
